\log x - \log y + \log y - \log z &= a + 15, \\
\log x - \log z &= a + 15. \\
\end{align*}
Notice that this is equivalent to the third equation, $\log z - \log x = -7$. Therefore, we can substitute the third equation into the above equation:
\begin{align*}
\log z - \log x &= -7, \\
\log x - \log z &= a + 15. \\
\end{align*}
By adding these two equations, we get:
\begin{align*}
\log x - \log z + \log z - \log x &= a + 15 - 7, \\
