x = \frac{3 \pm \sqrt{(-3)^2 - 4 \cdot 5 \cdot (-5)}}{2 \cdot 5} = \frac{3 \pm \sqrt{9 + 100}}{10} = \frac{3 \pm \sqrt{109}}{10}
\] This gives us two possible values for \(x\): \[
x = \frac{3 + \sqrt{109}}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad x = \frac{3 - \sqrt{109}}{10}
\] Next, we need to find the value of \((10x - 3)^2\). Let's consider both cases. If \(x = \frac{3 + \sqrt{109}}{10}\), then \(10x - 3 = 3 + \sqrt{109} - 3 = \sqrt{109}\), so \((10x - 3)^2 = (\sqrt{109})^2 = 109\). If \(x = \frac{3 - \sqrt{109}}{10}\), then \(10x - 3 = 3 - \sqrt{109} - 3 = -\sqrt{109}\), so \((10x - 3)^2 = (-\sqrt{109})^2 = 109\). Therefore, in both cases, \((10x - 3)^2 = 109\). </think> <answer>109</answer>

